WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.756
- Warning. The video you
are about to watch...

00:00:01.756 --> 00:00:03.265
- Do not try this at home!

00:00:03.265 --> 00:00:05.272
- Or this will happen to you.

00:00:05.272 --> 00:00:06.780
You okay Colin?

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.945
- Uhhh. Don't eat doughnuts. Ever.

00:00:10.945 --> 00:00:14.419
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:15.414
- Live and direct from Hollywood.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:16.346
- Another adventure.

00:00:16.346 --> 00:00:18.238
We're about to do some
doughnut shop telephone.

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:21.021
- We're gonna try to find
the best doughnuts in L.A.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.013
- What we're gonna do is
go to one doughnut shop...

00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:24.455
- And we're going to ask
them what their favorite

00:00:24.455 --> 00:00:26.264
doughnut is, and we're gonna
go to the next doughnut shop.

00:00:26.264 --> 00:00:27.361
- To the next doughnut shop.

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:28.742
- Until we find the best doughnut...

00:00:28.742 --> 00:00:29.860
- In all of Los Angeles.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.099
- Doughnuts are my weakness!

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:34.451
I'm on a lifestyle called
Paleo minus doughnuts.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:36.666
- It's all about the
Krispy Kreme. Krispy Kreme.

00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:38.339
- [Jordan] Ewww! Get out of here!

00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:39.673
- [Colin] Yeah, that's disgusting.

00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:40.160
- [Jordan] What?

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.282
- That's what we eat in Ohio.

00:00:42.282 --> 00:00:43.418
No! I shouldn't have said that.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:43.919
- He's a liar.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:45.484
- [Steven] What makes a good doughnut?

00:00:45.484 --> 00:00:47.433
- Freshness is obviously
the most important

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:48.369
thing with a doughnut.

00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:49.770
- Well yeah, you never
want a stale doughnut.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.644
- Fluffiness.

00:00:50.644 --> 00:00:52.147
- Sugar-to-dough ratio.

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:54.321
- I compare doughnut shops based on their

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:55.459
chocolate frosted doughnut.

00:00:55.459 --> 00:00:56.434
- [Steven] I say we do that!

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.425
- This doughnut looks perfect.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.051
- Mine looks like a heart
on the inside actually.

00:01:00.051 --> 00:01:02.164
- Awww, yeah! Your doughnut loves you.

00:01:02.164 --> 00:01:04.195
- Looks like they use some
authentic chocolate here.

00:01:04.195 --> 00:01:06.491
- And I watched her put
the chocolate on the top.

00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:08.767
- That's such a good doughnut.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.555
- Yeah, the sugar-to-dough
ratio is appropriate.

00:01:10.555 --> 00:01:13.907
- And it doesn't taste gritty!
I hate gritty doughnuts.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.553
- I don't think I've ever
had a doughnut this good.

00:01:15.553 --> 00:01:17.320
- That's because you like Krispy Kreme.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.311
- [Colin] You have doughnut
in your hair, Jordan!

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.160
- Donut Friend, be my friend.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.237
- Four out of five.

00:01:22.237 --> 00:01:23.700
- What? You've had a
better doughnut than this?

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.057
- No, but this is the
first doughnut place.

00:01:26.057 --> 00:01:28.718
I'm not gonna start out
with five out of five,

00:01:28.718 --> 00:01:30.769
and then just assume
there's no better doughnuts.

00:01:30.769 --> 00:01:32.618
- I'm into it, but I want to try

00:01:32.618 --> 00:01:34.773
the other crazy doughnuts they have.

00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:36.134
- Woah!

00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:38.389
- This one is called the Srirachosin.

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:39.689
- What is happening?

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:41.314
- It is like a range of emotions.

00:01:41.314 --> 00:01:43.834
- But it's actually pleasant.
I mean, it's a meal!

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.008
- You know like when you feed
information to a computer,

00:01:46.008 --> 00:01:48.608
it shuts down? That's like me right now.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.949
I'm gonna just reboot.

00:01:49.949 --> 00:01:52.469
- Internal error. Internal error.

00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:54.175
- Every time we go to a doughnut shop,

00:01:54.175 --> 00:01:56.024
we ask the people at that doughnut shop

00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:58.746
what their favorite
doughnut spot to eat at is

00:01:58.746 --> 00:01:59.864
when you're not here.

00:01:59.864 --> 00:02:00.920
- Donut Man in Glendora.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.704
- This is exactly what I wanted to hear!

00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:05.166
- Colin's already conked out.

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:07.036
He's in doughnut coma.

00:02:07.036 --> 00:02:08.174
- Doughnut delirium.

00:02:08.174 --> 00:02:09.230
- Hey, we're here!

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.429
- Huh?

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:11.709
(laughter)

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:14.574
- I've heard about this
place for a long time.

00:02:14.574 --> 00:02:16.016
My dad grew up out here.

00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:16.788
- Does he like it?

00:02:16.788 --> 00:02:17.784
- I don't know.

00:02:17.784 --> 00:02:20.262
- I feel like this place
is really, really on par

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:23.208
with making things look
really cool and crazy.

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:25.024
- Cheers! Cheers!

00:02:25.024 --> 00:02:27.089
- [Jordan] It's nice and light.

00:02:27.089 --> 00:02:28.714
- Dense and fluffy!

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:30.949
- Yeah! It's that weird
perfect combination

00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:32.635
that you don't see in
doughnuts very often.

00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:33.428
It's pretty cool.

00:02:33.428 --> 00:02:35.256
- Chocolate frosted doughnut is more like

00:02:35.256 --> 00:02:37.694
the auntie who consoles
you when you're down.

00:02:37.694 --> 00:02:41.961
- Next up, we got this strawberry
insanity situation here.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.297
- I feel like I'm eating
a bread bowl of soup,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.410
but instead of soup, it's strawberries.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.975
- Here!

00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:48.664
- You know what I just realized?

00:02:48.664 --> 00:02:49.417
- What?

00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:50.860
- You can't have too many doughnuts.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.363
- This isn't like tacos.

00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:55.350
Tacos I could eat all day
and you just get full.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.707
This, I feel like I might pop.

00:02:57.707 --> 00:02:59.047
- I'm doughn-ed out!

00:02:59.047 --> 00:02:59.779
(laughter)

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.050
- I dough-not want to
eat anymore doughnuts.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:03.578
- We got to do it!

00:03:03.578 --> 00:03:05.447
- Besides the doughnuts
here, where would you suggest

00:03:05.447 --> 00:03:08.434
that we should go to next, for
our next doughnut adventure?

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:11.928
- All my coworkers are
saying Lady's Donuts.

00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:13.411
- And Lady's Donuts is
right down the street.

00:03:13.411 --> 00:03:14.204
- Let's go!

00:03:14.204 --> 00:03:15.423
(clapping)

00:03:15.423 --> 00:03:16.499
- Lady's Donuts unfortunately didn't

00:03:16.499 --> 00:03:18.063
want to be on camera, so...

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:18.835
- We're asking the internet!

00:03:18.835 --> 00:03:20.929
- Twitter said California Donuts.

00:03:20.929 --> 00:03:22.392
- California Donuts, here we come!

00:03:22.392 --> 00:03:26.475
(surf music)

00:03:26.475 --> 00:03:27.633
- If I was a doughnut, I would be

00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:29.117
something like apple cinnamon.

00:03:29.117 --> 00:03:29.787
- I could see that.

00:03:29.787 --> 00:03:31.188
- Little bit of sweet,
little bit of spicy.

00:03:31.188 --> 00:03:33.179
- I'm a chocolate-covered
old fashioned doughnut.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:33.769
- Why chocolate-covered?

00:03:33.769 --> 00:03:35.191
- Because I like chocolate.

00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:36.817
- Ohhh!

00:03:36.817 --> 00:03:39.702
- I think I'd be maple bacon.

00:03:39.702 --> 00:03:41.957
Many layers to the doughnut,
many layers to my life.

00:03:41.957 --> 00:03:45.512
- I don't want to say a basic,
boring, old glazed doughnut,

00:03:45.512 --> 00:03:48.418
but I think I would be a
basic, boring, glazed doughnut.

00:03:48.418 --> 00:03:49.169
- [Freddie] Yes!

00:03:49.169 --> 00:03:49.895
- [Colin] I absolutely agree with that.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:50.653
- [Freddie] Absolutely.

00:03:50.653 --> 00:03:51.973
- We've got to try the basic one.

00:03:51.973 --> 00:03:56.006
- The one you connect most with.

00:03:56.006 --> 00:03:57.101
- It's really good.

00:03:57.101 --> 00:03:57.787
- It's a good donut.

00:03:57.787 --> 00:03:58.861
- This is like the kind of bread

00:03:58.861 --> 00:04:00.486
that you get at an Asian bakery.

00:04:00.486 --> 00:04:02.376
- You can tell it's quality dough.

00:04:02.376 --> 00:04:03.065
- Uh-huh.

00:04:03.065 --> 00:04:05.261
- But more bready than I
would prefer for a doughnut.

00:04:05.261 --> 00:04:08.755
- I would like to combine the
dough from California Donuts,

00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:11.721
with the chocolate glaze at Donut Man.

00:04:11.721 --> 00:04:13.347
- My pick is Donut Man in Glendora.

00:04:13.347 --> 00:04:14.749
I think that was a special doughnut.

00:04:14.749 --> 00:04:15.946
- This is my favorite doughnut.

00:04:15.946 --> 00:04:17.329
Doughnut shop telephone works.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:19.157
- I'm gonna have to say that Donut Friend

00:04:19.157 --> 00:04:20.702
had my favorite chocolate glaze.

00:04:20.702 --> 00:04:22.266
- I would say this doughnut wins

00:04:22.266 --> 00:04:24.480
on sugar-to-dough ratio alone.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.293
Let's get crazy!

00:04:25.293 --> 00:04:27.650
- I'm gonna get this
green tea one right here.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:28.442
- You don't like that?

00:04:28.442 --> 00:04:29.194
- No!

00:04:29.194 --> 00:04:30.047
- What's it taste like?

00:04:30.047 --> 00:04:32.261
- It tastes like ewww.

00:04:32.261 --> 00:04:34.944
- This is my favorite
doughnut of all time.

00:04:34.944 --> 00:04:35.755
- Ughhh.

00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:37.504
- That croissant?

00:04:37.504 --> 00:04:39.820
- Now I have had a maple
bacon cronut before,

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:40.673
but not from here.

00:04:40.673 --> 00:04:43.206
- [Jordan] Freddie, you look
like you're about to cry.

00:04:43.206 --> 00:04:44.371
- It's so good.

00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:45.082
- That's delicious!

00:04:45.082 --> 00:04:46.362
- Yeah, it's good.

00:04:46.362 --> 00:04:47.053
- That's really tasty.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.536
- It's the bacon. I think it's because

00:04:48.536 --> 00:04:50.567
I'm finally getting
some savory in my mouth.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:51.116
(laughter)

00:04:51.116 --> 00:04:53.534
- I have never pigged out on
anything else to this degree,

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.870
that made me feel as
awful as I do right now.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:56.967
- Doughnuts are no joke.

00:04:56.967 --> 00:04:58.958
I have been training
for this my whole life.

00:04:58.958 --> 00:05:01.518
I still eat at least six
doughnuts every weekend.

00:05:01.518 --> 00:05:04.789
- Yeah, doughnut delirium is
not an ideal state to be in,

00:05:04.789 --> 00:05:07.836
but if you're with people that
you love, it's all worth it.

00:05:07.836 --> 00:05:10.641
- Awww! You love me, Freddie?

00:05:10.641 --> 00:05:11.474
- Eh.

00:05:11.474 --> 00:05:13.973
- I love crazy, weird doughnuts!

00:05:13.973 --> 00:05:14.459
- Yeah.

00:05:14.459 --> 00:05:16.614
- You like the crazy doughnuts
like you like your crazy men?

00:05:16.614 --> 00:05:17.914
(laughter)

00:05:17.914 --> 00:05:18.849
- There you go!

